  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **China Cat Sunflower** (1 review): Reviewer enjoys the abundant, slamming psychedelic riffing in China Cat Sunflower [2]\n- **I Know You Rider** (1 review): The harmonious transition from China Cat into I Know You Rider is singled out as a favorite [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tomorrow Is Forever**: rare: 10 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd72-10-30.aud.cotsman.10915.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): audience recording; 27 songs; 196 min; rated 3.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the audience recording okay; Reviewer finds the audience recording nice for its era; Reviewer finds the tape very nice, with clear ambiance [2][3][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer prefers this tape's clarity of ambiance over the sound of the second Milwaukee night [4]\n- Unlike some nights, this show lacks a monster jam around Dark Star or The Other One; it is long, tight rock and roll [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd72-10-30.aud.cotsman.10915.sbeok.shnf**: source: Audience Recording [1]. Also: Reviewer says this audience tape came from Bear himself, part of a recent flood of fall '72 audience tapes; Reviewer says Bear supposedly made this tape [4][5]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by LiveGRATEFUL.net: [Grateful Dead 1972-10-30 Mon Ford Auditorium, Detroit, MI](https://www.livegrateful.net/post/1422476086014/grateful-dead-1972-10-30-mon-ford) [7]\n- Fan art by LiveGRATEFUL.net: [Grateful Dead 1971-10-30 Sat Taft Auditorium, Cincinnati, OH](https://www.livegrateful.net/post/1422476877076/grateful-dead-1971-10-30-sat-taft) [8]",
